6-11-07","week":10,"type":"reg","home":false,"opp":"ND","oppName":"Notre Dame Fighting Irish","result":"L","score":"31-24","values":[13,57,4.4,0,29,1,6,6,0,4,0,0]},{"id":"401858296","date":"2026-11-14","week":11,"type":"reg","home":true,"opp":"DUKE","oppName":"Duke Blue Devils","result":"W","score":"36-25","values":[8,23,2.9,1,8,2,20,10,0,20,0,0]}]}},"summaryLabel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"No. 6 Miami loses RB Marty Brown, WR Joshua Moore for season","description":"No. 6 Miami has lost running back CharMar \"Marty\" Brown (knee) and wide receiver Joshua Moore (upper body) for the rest of the season following last Saturday's win over Wake Forest.","published":"2026-09-21T14:42:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49998297/no-6-miami-loses-rb-marty-brown-wr-joshua-moore-season","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Notre Dame loses safety Luke Talich to injury in first quarter vs. SMU","description":"Notre Dame starting safety Luke Talich left the Fighting Irish's game against SMU in the first quarter with an apparent right leg injury suffered on the opening drive of the game Saturday night in South Bend, Indiana.","published":"2026-11-22T02:00:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556999/notre-dame-safety-luke-talich-exits-1st-half-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Which teams have the best odds to make the College Football Playoff?","description":"We are tracking the odds for making the CFP, earning a bye and winning it all.","published":"2026-11-22T01:42:15.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50532919/college-football-playoff-odds-predictions","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Brandon's two TD runs lift No. 9 Tennessee past LSU","description":"Tennessee's stifling defense shut down LSU, and the No. 9 Volunteers beat the Tigers 27-13 on Saturday to maintain their place in the College Football Playoff hunt.","published":"2026-11-22T01:48:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556758/brandon-two-td-runs-lift-no-9-tennessee-lsu","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Bryce Underwood makes most of second chance, sparks Michigan's upset of UCLA","description":"Reinserted as Michigan's starting quarterback earlier this week, Bryce Underwood threw a 3-yard 2-point conversion pass Jalen Hoffman, lifting the Wolverines to an 18-16 triple-overtime win over previously unbeaten No. 4 UCLA on Saturday night.","published":"2026-11-22T01:36:46.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556702/bryce-underwood-michigan-outlast-ucla-triple-over","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Nebraska's jab at Ohio State's 'THE' leads top Week 12 CFB trolls","description":"Nebraska deployed a simple but effective troll that poked fun at its opponent's propensity to emphasize the \"the\" in \"The Ohio State University.\"","published":"2026-11-22T01:12:49.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50554531/nebraska-ohio-state-trolls-college-football-week-12","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Indiana's CFP hopes take hit after OT loss at Washington","description":"Indiana might not get a chance to defend its national championship after losing 27-24 at Washington on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:14:52.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556327/indiana-cfp-hopes-take-hit-ot-loss-washington","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"UCLA loses Ty Dieffenbach to injury, stays resolute with B1G title game in reach","description":"UCLA coach Bob Chesney said his message to the Bruins was, \"Nobody hang your head,\" despite losing QB Ty Dieffenbach to injury in a tough, 18-16 defeat at Michigan on Saturday.","published":"2026-11-22T02:30:01.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50556107/ucla-qb-ty-dieffenbach-carted-3ot-loss-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Week 12 live: Tracking top moments and best highlights","description":"Tracking the top plays and developments from Week 12.","published":"2026-11-22T00:47:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50541394/week-12-live-highlights","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN staff","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Preseason No. 1 Ohio State suffers fourth loss, will 'evaluate what's going on'","description":"For coach Ryan Day and his Ohio State Buckeyes, the dream of a College Football Playoff run is dead, as the preseason No. 1 team in college football lost its fourth game on Saturday afternoon, a 31-28 decision at the hands of the Nebraska Cornhuskers.","published":"2026-11-22T00:30:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50555411/preseason-no-1-ohio-state-sees-cfp-hopes-end-4th-loss","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4870736/mark-fletcher-jr","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Fletcher_Jr."},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Mark Fletcher Jr.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mark_Fletcher_Jr.","description":"American football player (born 2004)","touched":"2026-11-14T07:36:32Z","intro":"Mark Fletcher Jr. (born October 17, 2004) is an American college football running back for the Miami Hurricanes.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Fletcher attended American Heritage School in Plantation, Florida. As a senior, he rushed for 1,934 yards and 23 touchdowns. Fletcher originally committed to Ohio State, before decommitting during his senior year. A four-star recruit, he committed to play college football at the University of Miami over an offer from Florida."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Fletcher made his Hurricanes debut in the 2023 season opener against Miami (Ohio), rushing for 76 yards on nine carries and a touchdown in a 38–3 victory. Against Virginia, he scored the game-winning touchdown in overtime in a 29–26 win. Against NC State, he rushed for 115 yards, marking his first 100-yard collegiate game, in a 20–6 loss. He ran for a season-high 126 yards and two touchdowns against Louisville in a 38–31 defeat. In the 2023 Pinstripe Bowl, Fletcher suffered a Lisfranc injury and was carted off the field. He finished his freshman season with 514 rushing yards and five touchdowns in ten games and four starts, missing three games due to other injuries.\nFletcher returned from injury for the 2024 season, playing in all 13 games and making four starts. He made an immediate impact in the season opener against Florida, rushing for two touchdowns in a 41–17 victory.\nIn 2025, Fletcher had back‑to‑back games with two rushing touchdowns in Miami’s victories over Bethune–Cookman and South Florida in Weeks 2 and 3. He recorded a career‑high three rushing touchdowns and 106 yards on 23 carries in a 42–7 win against Stanford. In the first round of the College Football Playoff against Texas A&M, Fletcher rushed for a career‑high 172 yards on 17 carries in a 10–3 victory. In the quarterfinal against Ohio State, he ran for 90 yards on 19 carries and was named the J. Curtis Sanford Offensive Most Valuable Player as the Hurricanes won 24–14. Fletcher continued his strong postseason run in the semifinal against Ole Miss, rushing for 133 yards on 22 carries in a 31–27 win. In the 2026 College Football Playoff National Championship against Indiana, Fletcher rushed for 112 yards and two touchdowns, including a career-long 57-yard score, in a 27–21 defeat. On the field after the game, he threw a punch at Indiana defensive lineman Tyrique Tucker. Fletcher finished the 2025 season having played in 14 games with 12 starts, rushing for an ACC‑leading 1,192 yards on 216 carries with a 5.5 average and 12 touchdowns, and was named third-team All-ACC."}]}}